# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so never
# put a real value here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only `tests/smoke_live.py` reads any of this. The offline suites
# (`tests/test_remote.py`, `tests/test_main.py`) need nothing set.


# The repository `tests/smoke_live.py` lists over the live GitHub API.
#
# It is configured rather than hardcoded for two reasons: this tree carries no
# third-party repository references, and what the test needs is a *property*
# rather than one specific URL. Any repo works if it is:
#
#   - public, and readable anonymously (the test sends no token)
#   - holding `.CT` / `.ct` tables as real git blobs, not Git LFS pointers
#     (`remote.is_lfs_pointer` will reject those, and the test will say so)
#   - small enough that one recursive tree listing is not truncated
#
# Best results come from a repo that is flat and mixes XML tables with pre-5.6
# binary ones: that mix is what `looks_like_legacy` exists to tell apart, and a
# name containing a space is what catches raw-URL percent-encoding bugs.
#
# Accepted forms: a full URL, `owner/repo`, or a `/tree/<branch>/<subdir>` URL.
# Unset, the test skips rather than fails.
#
# SMOKE_REPO=https://github.com/owner/repo
SMOKE_REPO=
